 "differences": [
  "The deposit's acoustic files are 48 kHz recordings, where the paper says the acoustic data were recorded at 44.1 kHz.",
  "The paper's Tables 3, 5 and 6 give the number of observations that entered each mixed model (for example 2,342 and 1,541 durations, and 760, 748, 783 and 782 closing movements): these follow residual-based trimming in the authors' models, which was not re-run, so only the counts of the data themselves are checked here.",
  "The paper says 16 utterances of one speaker had a different prosodic structure than targeted and were re-categorized; in the deposit the 16 words whose phrasal_position differs from the intended one (10 intended phrase-medial, 6 intended phrase-final, as in the paper's Table 2) come from 3 speakers (words per speaker: 14, 1, 1)."
 ],
